# FILESYSTEMS — ext2 / FAT / exFAT are never mounted here (no block driver: blk_* above refuse). vfs.cyr, klug.cyr's
# spill, shell.cyr and init.cyr test the *_active flags first, as on an x86 box with no such volume, and the functions
# refuse like x86's unmounted / unregistered paths (-1; a finder's "not found" 0; a lister's count 0). The leaf cursors and
# backends are the x86 vars' resting values; ext2_inode_buf keeps the x86 shape (32 u64 = one 256 B inode) so vfs.cyr's
# &ext2_inode_buf stays in bounds. modeset_latch_blocked (modeset_latch.cyr, x86) names klug's spill file — 0 = x86's
# default. ZFS (the zfs_active stubs above): no pool, so no path routes to FS_ZFS and the path readers refuse.
var ext2_active = 0;
var ext2_write_ok = 0;
var ext2_inode_buf[32];
var fat_on_esp = 0;
